<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Huan of Han</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">132–168</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Huan of Han was emperor of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> from 146 to 168. In 159 he used the palace <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuchs</a> to destroy the powerful consort clan of Liang Ji, after which eunuchs dominated the court, and in 166 he began the Partisan Prohibitions against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scholar-officials">scholar-officials</a> who opposed them. His reign saw frequent raids by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> under Tanshihuai.</p></div>
